  "body": "The modeled color progression shows stark regional variation. Southwest Lower Michigan leads at 94 percent with falling color, while Southeast Lower peaks at 96 percent. Central and Saginaw Bay regions show 58 percent in the falling phase. The Upper Peninsula and northern Lower Peninsula remain early, all at 7 to 10 percent in the down phase.\n\nThis weekend's mixed skies across most regions favor viewing, though rain affects the U.P. and Northeast Lower through the next few days. Temperatures range from highs near 57 to 70 degrees with lows between 32 and 44. The cooler nights in northern areas may accelerate color change, while milder conditions in the south support peak viewing windows.\n\nFor optimal foliage viewing this weekend, Southeast Lower Michigan along US-12 through the Irish Hills offers peak color conditions with favorable mixed skies and moderate temperatures. Alternatively, Southwest Lower's Blue Star Highway near Saugatuck provides near-peak color with similar weather patterns and slightly warmer conditions ideal for a scenic drive.",
